id: pm-tlr2dl
title: Investigate health drift verdicts during concurrent tracker writes
description: During the October24 merge delivery a long health scan reported history_drift_hash_mismatch for an item receiving normal PM evidence writes. A fresh per-item verifier immediately proved a valid15-event chain and exact current hash equality; a quiet health rerun also passed with no repair. This observation suggests a diagnostic read-consistency gap but does not yet establish a deterministic source-level reproduction. Preserve existing drift detection and distinguish real corruption from a changed revision.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: context-management,health,"horizon:near",read-consistency
created_at: "2026-10-24T20:41:50.937Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:14:42.616Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic isolated fixture reproduces or disproves the observed read/write interleaving; Real drift remains detectable and no diagnostic mutates item or history bytes; Concurrent changes are retried within a bounded budget or reported as an explicit consistency limitation; SDK and CLI acceptance preserve current health and verifier contracts
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make concurrent diagnostic reads report only conclusions supported by a coherent item/history revision
value: Prevent unnecessary history repair and preserve trustworthy context for concurrent agents
why_now: A live diagnostic disagreed with fresh strict verification while evidence writes were in flight
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "Diagnostics either verify a coherent item/history revision or explicitly disclose concurrent change with safe bounded recovery, while still detecting actual drift."
